Lab 1-
Document the following in your Week 2 lab notes:

Why the encrypted file is unreadable- for confidentiality

What would happen if the wrong password were used- you wouldn't be able to decrypt the file

What security property does symmetric encryption provide: confidentiality

Why TLS uses symmetric encryption for data transfer- it's faster 

lab 2-
Why the hash changed after a small modification- it wasn't the same as the original file 

Why hashing does NOT provide confidentiality- hashing doesn't keep anything confidential. It only runs a mathematical scan to see if things are the same in both the file and digital signature

What security property hashing provides- integrity

Where hashing is used in PKI systems- when they create and verify the digital signature 

lab 3- 
Why verification succeeds before tampering- this question didn't make any sense to me. I had to ask chat what it meant in lamen terms and it gave me this Why does the "seal" look perfect before anyone messes with the letter? Because the "mold" I used to make the seal (my Private Key) and the "template" you use to check it (my Public Key) are a perfect mathematical match. Since the paper didn't change, the "shape" of the message still fits the seal.
