## Mental Model

Short summary that ties the week back to:

Identity + Trust + Verification
Why verification fails after modification- because hashing let's me know it's been tampered with

Why digital signatures require both hashing and asymmetric cryptography- for double security no one can claim something they're not with more than one control in place

How this relates to certificate signing in PKI- CAs create the digital signature and that's what you hash against. 
